# Player art - original 16-bit pixel art (SNES-class). All frames face RIGHT, side view (profile).
# 1-px dark outline around every silhouette, 2-3 step shading ramps per material, light from the top-left.
# One set of images serves Mario / Luigi / Fire / Tanooki / Hammer / star flashing, so EVERY player palette
# uses the same 15-slot layout (always give all 15 entries):
#   1 outline   2 hair / mustache / eye   3 4 5 cap + shirt (hi, base, shade)   6 7 8 skin (hi, base, shade)
#   9 a b overalls (hi, base, shade)   c d shoes (base, shade)   e buttons / tail tip / accent   f white
# Overlays follow the same layout: ears/tails = 2 stripes, 3-5 fur, 6-8 inner ear, e tip; hood = 3-5 fur;
# helmet/shells = 9-b shell, 3-5 rims; frog = 3-5 green, 9-b belly, 2 pupils/mouth; statue = 3-5 stone.
# Body frames are wider/taller than the player box so no pose is cropped: big mb.* = 24x36, small ms.* = 20x20.
# The engine centres them on the 16-wide box and bottom-aligns them, so box column c = image column c+4 (big) /
# c+2 (small) and box row r = image row r+4. Feet stand on the last image row (outline row = the ground line).
# Head (box coords): cap top row 2 over columns 3-14, brim row 5, face rows 6-10 (small: cap rows 0-2, face 3-7).
# Big body: athletic - broad shoulders rows 11-15, tapered waist, hips row 21, long legs 22-27, shoes 28-30.
# Frames were composed from SMB3-inspired parts with per-material ramps;
# the front sleeve/hand get an internal outline, the far arm/leg use the darker end of their ramps.
# Overlay anchors live in src/Game/Player/PlayerDraw.cs (Anchor / TailAttach):
#   standard big frames: head overlays at y+1 (hy = 1): ears at y-2, hood/helmet at y+1.
#   mb.walk1 / mb.run1 / mb.run3 (stride frames) bob 1 px down; P-run head leans 1 px forward (x+1).
#   mb.skid: leaning back -> head overlays at x-1.
#   mb.duck / mb.slide: head lowered -> head overlays at y+12 / y+14; tail uses tail.mid.
#   mb.front / mb.spinfront (front view) and mb.climb* / mb.spinback (back view) use ears.front / helmet.front.
#   tails: base on the right edge, attach point (14,5) tail.down, (14,7) tail.mid, (14,10) tail.up,
#   joined to the rump point (4,21) of the standard frames (per-frame values in Anchor).
#   tail.side points RIGHT with its base on the left (drawn at x+12, y+20); tail.back hangs over the legs (back view).
#   mb.skid faces the NEW direction (feet braced toward the slide), matching Facing = input during a skid.
#   held shell is drawn by the engine at x+11 (y+13 big, y+17 small): hold frames put the hands at its left edge.
#                1 outline 2 hair   3 cap/shirt hi..shade    6 skin hi..shade        9 overalls hi..shade    c shoe  d shoe-sh e accent f white
pal mario      #200C14 #4A2410 #FF6860 #D82020 #8C1010 #FFE0B8 #F8B070 #C07040 #6890F8 #3050D0 #182880 #9A5020 #5A2808 #F8D830 #FFFFFF
# Luigi: green cap/shirt, navy overalls
pal luigi      #0C1418 #3A2410 #78E860 #28A838 #106820 #FFE0B8 #F8B070 #C07040 #5868C0 #28348C #121A4C #9A5020 #5A2808 #F8D830 #FFFFFF
# Fire: white cap/shirt, red overalls
pal fire       #200C14 #4A2410 #FFFFFF #E0D8E8 #9890B0 #FFE0B8 #F8B070 #C07040 #FF7060 #D82020 #8C1010 #9A5020 #5A2808 #F8D830 #FFFFFF
# Tanooki: full brown fur suit (3-5 suit, 9-b legs, c-d paws, e tan tail tip); hood, ears and tail use it too
pal tanooki    #1C0C08 #3A1C08 #E0A060 #B06828 #704018 #FFE0B8 #F8B070 #C07040 #C88848 #985020 #603010 #6A3810 #3A1C08 #F8D8A0 #FFFFFF
# Raccoon tail + ears: orange fur, dark stripes, cream tip / inner ear
pal tail       #1C0C08 #3A1C08 #F8A850 #D87020 #904010 #FFE8C8 #F8C890 #C89058 #F8A850 #D87020 #904010 #6A3810 #3A1C08 #FFF0D0 #FFFFFF
pal frog       #081808 #183018 #88F070 #30B040 #107028 #FFE0B8 #F8B070 #C07040 #FFF8C8 #E8D880 #B0A048 #30B040 #107028 #F8D830 #FFFFFF
# Hammer Suit: light shirt, dark slate suit / helmet / shell with steel rims
pal hammersuit #0C0C14 #4A2410 #FFFFFF #C8C8D8 #8080A0 #FFE0B8 #F8B070 #C07040 #7880A0 #465068 #222838 #465068 #222838 #F8D830 #FFFFFF
# Tanooki statue (stone)
pal statue     #181820 #505060 #E0E0E8 #A8A8B8 #707080 #E0E0E8 #A8A8B8 #707080 #E0E0E8 #A8A8B8 #707080 #A8A8B8 #707080 #C8C8D8 #FFFFFF
# Star-power flashing (cycled with the plain and fire palettes) and the power-up flash
pal pstar.1    #201008 #704010 #FFF8A0 #F8D030 #C08010 #FFF0D0 #F8D8A0 #D0A060 #FFA850 #F87010 #B04008 #C06010 #803008 #FFFFFF #FFFFFF
pal pstar.2    #081810 #184028 #E8FFE8 #80F090 #30A850 #FFFFFF #F0F0D8 #C8C8A8 #80F8F0 #20C8C8 #108080 #108080 #084848 #FFFFFF #FFFFFF
pal pflash     #402818 #906040 #FFFFFF #FFF0D0 #F8C890 #FFFFFF #FFF0D0 #F8C890 #FFFFFF #FFF0D0 #F8C890 #F8C890 #C89058 #FFFFFF #FFFFFF

